class:: HPCPEntropy
summary:: Normalized pitch-class distribution entropy
categories:: UGens>Analysis>Tonal
related:: Guides/MIRa, Classes/HPCP, Classes/HarmonicPeaks, Classes/Pitch2

description::
Computes Shannon entropy -sum(p*log(p))/log(N), after normalizing the nonnegative input to sum 1. Silence returns zero. A single occupied class gives zero; a uniform vector gives one. This is a general distribution statistic applied to tonal evidence, not a measure of musical sophistication or correctness.



classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: chroma
A C-first Array of 12, 24, 36, or 120 nonnegative pitch-class values. Higher resolutions fold to nearest semitones where a twelve-class representation is required.

argument:: trig
A positive value processes this control block. For FFT-derived features pass chain >= 0 so each analysis frame is used once; default 1 processes each control block.

returns::
Normalized entropy from 0 through 1.

examples::
HPCPEntropy computes the normalized Shannon entropy of pitch-class distribution (0 for a single isolated pitch class, 1 for equal uniform distribution across all 12 classes). Consonant simple triads have low entropy; dense cluster chords or atonal passages have high entropy. In this example, pitch-class entropy controls a diffuse granular delay scatter: simple triads remain clean and dry, while dissonant chords dissolve into an atmospheric cloud. An interactive code::MIRaGUI.scope:: displays real-time HPCP entropy.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIRaGUI.soundPath("piano-chords.wav");
    ~miraBuffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~miraBus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~miraExample = {
        var source = if(~miraBuffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic chords fallback
            Mix.ar(SinOsc.ar([261.63, 329.63, 392.00, 523.25] * LFNoise0.kr(0.5).range(1, 1.25))) * 0.15
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(2048), source, 0.25);
        var chroma = HPCP.kr(chain, size: 12, harmonics: 2, normalize: \max, fftSize: 2048);
        var entropy = HPCPEntropy.kr(chroma, chain >= 0);
        var entLag = entropy.lag(0.08);
        var scatter = CombC.ar(source, 0.2, SinOsc.kr([0.3, 0.4]).range(0.03, 0.1), 0.8) * entLag * 0.4;
        var direct = source * (1 - (entLag * 0.4));
        var sound = (direct ! 2 * 0.25) + scatter;

        if(~miraBus.notNil) { Out.kr(~miraBus, entLag.clip(0, 1)) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2)
    }.play;

    ~miraGUI = MIRaGUI.scope("HPCP Entropy", ~miraBus, 0.0, 1.0, "norm");
});
)
::
code::
(
~miraExample.free;
if(~miraGUI.notNil) { ~miraGUI.close };
if(~miraBus.notNil) { ~miraBus.free };
if(~miraBuffer.notNil) { ~miraBuffer.free };
)
::
